To terminate a C program, you can use the `exit()` function from the standard library `<stdlib.h>`. This function terminates the execution of the program and returns an integer value to the environment from which the program was launched.

Here's a basic example:

```c
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    // Terminate the program with exit code 0 (success)
    exit(0);
}
```

In this example, the program prints "Hello, World!" and then exits successfully with an exit code of 0.

